  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math> be two unit vectors such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>.&nbsp;If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is the angle between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>, then among the statements:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;: The projection of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math>&nbsp;on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mover><mi>a</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mover><mi>b</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "Only&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is true.",
